WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.069
the Dominican Republic isn't your
average Caribbean island it's a vibrant

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:10.019
place rich in culture and full of life
and although it may be known for its

00:00:10.019 --> 00:00:15.990
sandy beaches the island is home to an
array of landscapes climates and natural

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.150
wonders this is an island full of
surprises

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:31.619
the first is a sight that is invisible
to most travelers of the cursed of Punta

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:36.239
Cana sits one of the country's most
unique museums a museum full of history

00:00:36.239 --> 00:00:42.239
and life it can only be found over 20
feet underwater divers have the chance

00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:46.559
to explore a 17th century shipwreck as
it sits within the Caribbean reef in

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:52.890
this living museum of the sea the museum
was inaugurated in May of 2019 and since

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.840
then visitors have explored rare coral
shells turtles and fish while navigating

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.960
around cannons anchors and other
artifacts from a historic shipwreck the

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:08.040
area is protected from commercial
fishing and non recreational diving the

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:13.110
restrictions preserve maritime heritage
and help increase fish populations the

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.430
museum is just a short boat ride and
scuba dive away from the coast it's not

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.360
only a recreational dive site
it also shows rich histories and

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:28.860
flourishing biology's of the Dominican
Republic a next spot is one of the

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.900
largest protected areas in the country

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:38.070
along the Dominican Republic's northeast
coast is one of the country's crown

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:44.940
jewels las its's National Park los ITSs
which translates to mountainous land is

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:49.260
home to lush rainforests stunning
mangroves caves adorned with petroglyphs

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:54.330
and hundreds of bird species loss I
tesis was established as a national park

00:01:54.330 --> 00:02:00.750
in 1976 it covers an area of over 618
square miles so it's no wonder the

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:05.580
park's rainforests were a filming
location for Jurassic Park from the 100

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:09.390
foot rock formations suddenly jutting
out of the water two different caves and

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:13.680
mangroves the park is home to some
incredibly diverse habitats while las

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.760
itss is in a remote part of the island
many visitors make the journey to

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:23.970
experience the beauty and variety of
landscapes once inside they can hike or

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:29.030
kayak their way through the massive park

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:36.330
next up is a canyon short to spark a bit
of curiosity within the mountains and

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.100
winding river system just outside the
town of Cabarete is one of the country's

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:47.580
most unique sites the magic mushroom a
curiously shaped Canyon it's rounded at

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:51.239
the top and thinning at the bottom
giving it the appearance of a mushroom

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:55.330
cap
after a 45-minute drive from town to the

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:59.800
canyon entrance visitors hike and swim
through the jungle for full reaching

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.850
magic mushroom along the way there are
ample opportunities to cliff jump of

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:10.120
some of the Caribbeans most spectacular
waterfalls once visitors reach the magic

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:16.540
mushroom they can rappel down almost 200
feet into the freshwater streams while

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:21.010
hiking to magic mushroom visitors will
come across gorgeous spectacular

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:30.640
waterfalls and beautifully sculpted rock
formations we're still on the northern

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:38.709
coast but this time we're high up the
province of Puerto Plata is home to one

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:44.170
of the country's most iconic sights
Mount Isabel de Torres visitors have the

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:48.010
option to hike their way up or take the
Caribbeans first-ever cable car to the

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:55.570
top the cable car was built in 1975 and
brings visitors up over 2,600 feet above

00:03:55.570 --> 00:04:00.700
sea level to the highest point in puerto
plata atop the mountain there is a

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:05.049
replica of the iconic Christ the
Redeemer statue that was erected in 1917

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:09.489
and panoramic views of Puerto Plata
rolling green hills and the Atlantic

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:13.000
Ocean
beyond the sights from the top there is

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:19.049
a botanical garden at the peak full of
lush greenery and rare tropical flowers

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:24.280
Mount Isabel de Torres is the main
attraction within the Isabel de Torres

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.630
National Park it is the most visited
national park in all of the Dominican

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:34.600
Republic and last we venture south to
shake things up in a place that looks

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.830
far different than the others

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:43.280
on the southern coast of the island in
the last calderas Peninsula the

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:47.330
Dominican Republic's landscape
transforms into a stretch of desert like

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:52.940
fields known as the dunes of Bonny the
arid climate and topography contrasts

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:57.320
sharply from other regions in the
country the sand itself is very smooth

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:02.450
due to the abundance of quartz and
feldspar and the area is full of endemic

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:09.560
flora the June stretch over nine miles
and the tallest dune is over 114 feet

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:14.980
high the dunes of Bonny are the largest
sand dunes in all of the Caribbean in

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:19.430
1996 these genes were declared a
national monument visitors can walk

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:23.120
through the dunes or if they are
adventurous enough ride down on a sand

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:29.450
board the landscape feeds directly into
the ocean as the dunes are located right

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:35.260
next to playa Salinas

